[{:db/id -1
  :adr/addendum-2026-07-13d
  "Fixed the audit-tooling bug addendum-c found, rather than auditing another page
  (90-docs/design-quality/coscientist/iteration-04.md). Added score-site to
  90-docs/design-quality/audit.cljc: takes a page's parts ({:html ... :css
  string-or-vector :js ...}) instead of one pre-assembled string, detects
  <link rel=stylesheet href=...> in the HTML via external-stylesheet-hrefs (handles
  quoted and bare attribute values), and sets :incomplete? true + a :warning naming the
  unaccounted-for hrefs when no :css was supplied to cover them -- so the exact
  addendum-c mistake (scoring kami-creative-studio's index.html alone, silently missing
  its external public/css/ui.css) is now caught by the tool itself instead of requiring
  a human to notice. score-page (single-string) is unchanged and used internally after
  assembly; audit now calls score-site per page (existing plain-string callers are
  unaffected) and surfaces a top-level :incomplete list of any flagged page names.
  Regression-checked: grepped every previously-audited file for external stylesheets
  BEFORE touching code -- none of the 5 prior 100/100 pages (4 samples + kami-studio)
  use one, so those scores were never at risk from this bug class. Reproduced the exact
  addendum-c bug as a test case (score-site without :css -> 67.72/incomplete?=true/
  warning naming css/ui.css; with :css -> 66.59/incomplete?=nil), confirming the fix
  catches what previously required manual discovery. Separately (not a bug in this
  fix): re-running a full 6-page convergence check initially showed kami-creative-studio
  regressed to 5 findings -- root cause was the superproject's shared checkout at
  orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-creative-studio/public/ being gitignored build output never
  rebuilt there since addendum-c's fix landed (the fix build+verify+audit all happened
  inside the now-deleted isolated worktree). Confirmed the fix really is on main (commit
  966d445, merge 7c0439e) and rebuilt public/ in the shared checkout (shadow-cljs
  release + pages build) to get a fresh, accurate reading -- not a regression, but a
  reminder that gitignored build artifacts in a shared checkout silently go stale.
  Final state: all 6 pages this system has ever audited (4 samples, kami-studio,
  kami-creative-studio via the corrected score-site path) = 100.00/100, 0 findings,
  :incomplete? correctly nil on every one."
  :adr/addendum-2026-07-13c
  "Kaizen pass on kami-studio + kami-creative-studio (90-docs/design-quality/coscientist/
  iteration-03.md), landing the addendum-b findings for real. Before shipping, found a
  SECOND real audit-methodology bug: kami-creative-studio's actual CSS lives in a
  separately-linked public/css/ui.css, not inlined in public/index.html -- audit.cljc's
  score-page takes one string, so the addendum-b run (index.html alone) never saw the
  real styling. Concatenating index.html+ui.css gave a corrected baseline of 66.59/100
  (not 67.72) with a materially different finding set (overflow-guard/responsive were
  false negatives; reduced-motion was a newly-surfaced real gap). Also found: this app
  is client-side-rendered, so tap-targets/focus-visible's <button>/<input> literal-tag
  regex structurally false-positives (matches nothing in static files since all markup
  is JS-generated at runtime) -- verified by hand-grepping ui.cljs instead of trusting
  the tool: tap-targets was genuinely fine ($button already had min-height:44px) but
  focus-visible was a REAL unmeasured gap (only $input had :focus, not :focus-visible;
  $button/$trait-card/$file had none). Documented as a standing limitation of
  design-quality.audit for CSR apps, not fixed this pass. Shipped via isolated git
  worktrees (kami-studio 83edddf->c6143d6, no test suite, verified via re-render+
  re-audit; kami-creative-studio 6fc4a1c->7c0439e, existing 6 tests/23 assertions green,
  full local build via npm install + shadow-cljs release (0 warnings) + pages build,
  confirmed the compiled CSS actually contains every fix before re-auditing), merged
  server-side, worktrees/branches cleaned up. Results: kami-studio 50.75->100.00/100 (7
  findings fixed: viewport-fit, safe-area all 4 edges, focus-visible, theme-color+
  color-scheme, overflow-x guard, responsive breakpoint, html lang -- also reformatted
  the 1-line source into readable multi-line hiccup, no functional change).
  kami-creative-studio 66.59->100.00/100 (viewport-fit, color-scheme, safe-area on both
  fixed top/bottom bars, the real focus-visible gap found by hand, a hand-written global
  prefers-reduced-motion reset since shadow-css's per-class @media syntax can't express
  a universal-selector rule). One honest documented limitation: kami-creative-studio's
  $top safe-area-inset-top padding grows the header box outward (content-box, no global
  border-box reset) rather than clipping content, but $workspace's calc(100vh - 54px)
  doesn't account for the extra height, so a notched device could clip a few dozen px off
  the workspace grid's bottom -- follow-up noted, not silently claimed as perfect. west.yml
  registration remains out of scope; both fixes are landed on each repo's own main
  regardless of manifest status. 20 more ledger lines appended (10 audit rows per app, all
  1.0, design-quality-studios-kaizen-20260713-0942 run)."
  :adr/addendum-2026-07-13b
  "Extended scoring to kotoba-lang/kami-studio + kotoba-lang/kami-creative-studio (user
  asked for 'kotoba-studio'/'kotoba-creative-studio', which do not exist -- gh repo list
  confirmed only kami-studio/kami-creative-studio exist; both were already manually
  cloned under orgs/kotoba-lang/ but unregistered in west.yml/repos.edn). Neither uses
  kotoba-ui/liquid-glass-ui/uikit/appkit at all (kami-studio: kotoba-lang/html+css only;
  kami-creative-studio: reagent+shadow-cljs+kotoba-lang/kisekae+model-viewer), so the
  :lint layer doesn't apply. Added :audit layer (9 axes, design-quality.audit,
  deterministic) to the catalog for the first time (previously only used ad-hoc via
  coscientist.cljc, never fed into the ledger) + 2 new :lib entries + an adapted
  3-judge :llm-judge panel (consistency axis redefined as internal self-consistency,
  no sibling-family comparison). Results: kami-studio audit 50.75/100, judges clarity
  4.07/deference 4.33/depth 3.23/consistency 4.57/token-discipline 3.00 (n=3).
  kami-creative-studio audit 67.72/100, judges clarity 4.00/deference 4.00/depth
  3.50/consistency 4.00/token-discipline 3.00 (n=2, 1 judge failed structured-output
  retry). Cross-signal finding: token_discipline scored 3.00/5 on BOTH apps (vs
  4.5-4.93 for the kotoba-ui-family libraries) and the audit's color-scheme axis
  independently flags both as missing theme-color/color-scheme -- two independent
  measurement layers agree these apps lack any token/CSS-variable layer, pointing at
  adopting kotoba-ui.theme/shitsuke.tokens as the highest-leverage improvement for
  both. 30 ledger lines appended (18 audit + 10 llm-judge-mean; raw per-judge scores
  were not preserved by this round's workflow design, mean-only -- a gap vs the
  original 4-library workflow's full traceability, noted as a process improvement for
  next time). Formal west.yml/repos.edn registration of these 2 repos is out of scope
  for this scoring-only pass."
  :adr/addendum-2026-07-13
  "Co-Scientist kaizen pass (isekai.ux ADR-0007 移植, keiei-arbor-coscientist-engine
  ADR-2606141500 が原典). Added deterministic fitness function
  90-docs/design-quality/audit.cljc (isekai.ux.audit port, no LLM/browser, 9 axes) +
  90-docs/design-quality/coscientist.cljc (isekai.ux.coscientist port, offline/heuristic
  Generate->Reflect->Rank(Elo)->Evolve->Meta, no langchain-clj dep). Iteration 01
  (90-docs/design-quality/coscientist/iteration-01.md): baseline 71.55/100 across the 4
  sample pages -- the SAME libraries the 3-judge llm-judge panel scored 4.0-5.0/5 on every
  HIG axis, yet no judge flagged any of: missing min-height>=44px on
  .liquid-glass__button/.liquid-glass__icon-button (tap-targets w=0.13), no dvh fallback on
  .kotoba-shell__app (dynamic-viewport w=0.09), only bottom safe-area-inset covered not top
  (safe-area w=0.13), no <meta theme-color> (color-scheme w=0.06), no viewport-fit=cover
  (viewport w=0.10), no max-width media query on the liquid-glass-ui showcase (responsive
  w=0.07, that page only). Elo-ranked (predicted-gain is the judge, no LLM debate), shipped
  the 4 consumer-fixable low-risk findings as unlayered app CSS batch
  design-quality-kaizen-1 via generate-samples.cljs's :head opt (no shared orgs/kotoba-lang/*
  checkout edited). Re-measured: 71.55 -> 90.38/100 (+18.83; the 3 shipped samples each
  71.14->96.25, the untouched liquid-glass-ui showcase page stayed flat at 72.77 as the
  control proving the delta is real). viewport (kotoba-ui.shell/page hardcodes a single
  meta tag with no :head override point) and responsive (needs editing the showcase page
  itself) were deferred as upstream-only follow-ups in iteration 01.

  Iteration 02 (90-docs/design-quality/coscientist/iteration-02.md) landed both deferred
  findings for real via isolated git worktrees outside the superproject (kotoba-ui and
  liquid-glass-ui each), verified against each repo's own test suite (20 tests/130
  assertions; 59 tests/632 assertions, both green) before pushing, merged server-side
  (gh api .../merges, no local rebase/force-push), manifest/west.yml pins advanced via
  nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry <name> (minimal per-entry diff, verified,
  no wholesale regen). This round caught a REAL bug in the loop itself before shipping:
  heuristic-hypothesis's fix text is generic per-axis and doesn't verify the proposed
  CSS selector exists on the actual target page -- it proposed
  .kotoba-shell__app{min-height:100dvh} for the liquid-glass-ui showcase page, which
  doesn't use kotoba-ui.shell at all (grep -c kotoba-shell__app docs/index.html == 0);
  shipping it as-worded would have been a dead no-op fix. Caught by checking the real
  markup before shipping, then applying the correct selectors (body, and the page's
  actually-present .liquid-glass__nav-bar). Final measured state after 3 audit rounds:
  71.55 -> 90.38 -> 95.16 -> 100.00/100, 0 findings across all 4 pages (converged on the
  current 9-axis rubric). Added a converged-state branch to coscientist.cljc's
  iteration-md (isekai's own iteration-07 pattern) so future re-runs at 0 findings report
  honestly instead of rendering empty tables. Iteration 03 seed: fix
  heuristic-hypothesis to verify selectors against real page content, add a WCAG 1.4.3
  contrast-ratio axis, wire a real screenshot-critic lens into Generate, consider
  promoting the nav-bar safe-area-top fix from demo-page-only into liquid-glass.style
  itself."
  :adr/closing-summary-2026-07-13
  "Closed at user's 'closing' instruction. Final state: 6 pages ever audited by this
  system (4 samples + kami-studio + kami-creative-studio) = 100.00/100, 0 findings.
  6 repos landed real merged fixes on their own main (kotoba-ui, liquid-glass-ui,
  kami-studio, kami-creative-studio, plus 2 manifest/west.yml pin advances in
  com-junkawasaki/root). 3 real tool bugs found and self-caught before shipping: (1)
  heuristic-hypothesis doesn't verify selectors against real page markup -- UNFIXED,
  top priority for a future session (it proposed a dead no-op CSS rule once, caught by
  hand before shipping). (2) design-quality.audit's single-string API silently
  undercounted pages with externally-linked CSS -- FIXED via score-site (addendum-d).
  (3) tap-targets/focus-visible structurally false-positive on client-rendered SPAs --
  documented as a standing limitation, not fixed. Open backlog for next session, in
  priority order: fix heuristic-hypothesis's selector-verification gap; add a real
  WCAG 1.4.3 contrast-ratio axis (seeded 3 iterations running); formalize/fix the CSR
  blind spot; make :sample-visual a real 3-judge panel (currently single-pass); decide
  whether to register kami-studio/kami-creative-studio in manifest/west.yml (left out
  of scope deliberately)."
